You think so?

257
00:13:50,250 --> 00:13:53,420
I hope you find Page.

258
00:13:53,420 --> 00:13:54,080
Well, see yah!

259
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:56,250
Thanks. Take care.

260
00:14:11,940 --> 00:14:15,370
In order to survive, without realizing it,

261
00:14:15,370 --> 00:14:18,600
I've adapted myself
to society's expectations.

262
00:14:21,950 --> 00:14:24,450
"If you live life by
other people's standards,

263
00:14:24,450 --> 00:14:28,910
then your life is no longer yours."
That's what Eddy said.

264
00:14:36,130 --> 00:14:40,060
If I really thought about what
it means to live life and to die,

265
00:14:40,060 --> 00:14:44,060
I may be the one who needs
to reassess things.

266
00:16:11,590 --> 00:16:16,590
What?! Page was singing along with you?
Then it must be a great song!

267
00:16:16,590 --> 00:16:19,930
Yeah, but I've only gotten
part of the refrain done.

268
00:16:19,930 --> 00:16:20,600
Hmm...

269
00:16:20,600 --> 00:16:24,270
If he didn't interrupt, I think I would
have had the whole song finished.

270
00:16:24,270 --> 00:16:28,030
But after struggling to
catch Page, it all went away.

271
00:16:29,610 --> 00:16:30,800
It just came to you?

272
00:16:32,280 --> 00:16:36,010
It seems so strange
when I think of it now.

273
00:16:37,210 --> 00:16:41,890
When I was trying to compose
a song, I couldn't at all.

274
00:16:41,890 --> 00:16:44,880
Then all of a sudden,
this melody just popped up in my head.

275
00:16:47,220 --> 00:16:50,890
Well, let's hear it!

276
00:16:50,890 --> 00:16:51,950
Okay.

277
00:17:36,540 --> 00:17:40,040
Koyuki, you really wrote that tune?

278
00:17:40,040 --> 00:17:40,980
Uh-huh.

279
00:17:46,050 --> 00:17:48,050
Then, where should I go?

280
00:17:48,050 --> 00:17:53,080
Okay, I know that. What time?
Okay. I'll be there.

281
00:18:18,420 --> 00:18:21,410
Hey, It's my first time
to ride on a helicopter.

282
00:18:25,420 --> 00:18:27,390
I brought this again, for Beck. Take it.

283
00:18:27,390 --> 00:18:28,790
"Dog Arnold's Bone" [Doggie Treats]

284
00:18:27,390 --> 00:18:28,790
I brought this again, for Beck. Take it.

285
00:18:28,790 --> 00:18:30,930
Hey, you fuckin' talk too much.

286
00:18:30,930 --> 00:18:32,430
Shoot me if you want, all right?

287
00:18:32,430 --> 00:18:35,430
You think I won't shoot you
right here, muthafucker?

288
00:18:35,430 --> 00:18:39,270
Hey, stop it! We're talking business here.

289
00:18:42,370 --> 00:18:44,880
So, where are you going?

290
00:18:44,880 --> 00:18:46,710
North.

291
00:18:46,710 --> 00:18:49,740
Damn, fucker! Always getting me
in trouble with the boss.

292
00:19:13,070 --> 00:19:16,230
Yukio! It's your favorite, stew!

293
00:19:28,090 --> 00:19:30,550
Damn, this fucker's
always doing this shit...

294
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:49,710
Hello. Good morning.
Do you know who this is?

295
00:19:49,710 --> 00:19:51,880
There's only one woman that I know

296
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:53,880
with a whiskey-soaked,
raspy voice like yours.

297
00:19:53,880 --> 00:19:55,050
It's been decided.

298
00:19:55,050 --> 00:19:58,850
You guys will be going on
the Grateful Sound stage.

299
00:19:58,850 --> 00:19:59,720
Yeah.

300
00:19:59,720 --> 00:20:04,720
There was a real push from Leon.
Even Ran couldn't resist.

301
00:20:04,720 --> 00:20:07,220
Hey Aunty, it's not finalized yet.

302
00:20:07,220 --> 00:20:09,230
Huh? What do you mean?

303
00:20:09,230 --> 00:20:11,730
I still have to run it
by the rest of the band.

304
00:20:11,730 --> 00:20:15,730
But don't you guys want to
perform at Grateful Sound?

305
00:20:15,730 --> 00:20:19,400
Yesterday, I met with Leon.
We even went to look at the stage.

306
00:20:19,400 --> 00:20:22,070
So...what happened?

307
00:20:22,070 --> 00:20:24,410
His terms were way too hard.

308
00:20:24,410 --> 00:20:27,000
I don't think we can go through with it.

309
00:20:32,580 --> 00:20:34,580
Hello, Ryusuke-kun?

310
00:20:34,580 --> 00:20:38,690
What's up? Koyuki, come help me
set up the fishing poles.

311
00:20:38,690 --> 00:20:41,280
Umm, I wanted you to listen to this.

312
00:21:10,720 --> 00:21:15,060
Hmm. I'm surprised
you wrote such a tune.

313
00:21:15,060 --> 00:21:16,060
Really?

314
00:21:16,060 --> 00:21:19,730
But the continuity is off.

315
00:21:19,730 --> 00:21:20,860
I see.

316
00:21:38,750 --> 00:21:42,090
All right! I've decided, Koyuki.

317
00:21:42,090 --> 00:21:43,420
Hmm? Decided what?

318
00:21:45,420 --> 00:21:49,430
We're going to appear at Grateful Sound!

319
00:21:49,430 --> 00:21:59,600
H-Hey! I-I-Is this for real?!
U-Us! Hah-hah!

320
00:21:59,600 --> 00:22:01,270
-Yeah!
-Dying Breed's not appearing?

321
00:22:01,270 --> 00:22:04,110
No, I don't want to trouble Eddy.

322
00:22:04,110 --> 00:22:08,510
I see. So what were Leon's terms?

323
00:22:11,110 --> 00:22:13,450
We'll talk about it later.

324
00:22:13,450 --> 00:22:16,280
Right now, I just want to focus
on improving the band's skills.

325
00:22:20,960 --> 00:22:23,130
Chiba-kun! I'm sure
they'll give you one if you ask.

326
00:22:23,130 --> 00:22:24,920
Yeah, is that so?

327
00:22:27,630 --> 00:22:29,130
You sure like to pilfer stuff.

328
00:22:29,130 --> 00:22:30,690
Shut up, you!

329
00:22:33,970 --> 00:22:35,700
An incredible summer...

330
00:22:37,740 --> 00:22:40,610
A really incredible summer
is about to unfold...

331
00:22:43,440 --> 00:22:48,810
Full moon sways

332
00:22:50,280 --> 00:22:56,290
Gently in the night of one fine day

333
00:22:56,290 --> 00:22:58,990
What a fool

334
00:22:58,990 --> 00:23:02,460
I don't know 'bout tomorrow

335
00:23:02,460 --> 00:23:07,300
What it's like to be

336
00:23:07,300 --> 00:23:09,290
Ah...

337
00:23:10,470 --> 00:23:12,310
I was fool

338
00:23:12,310 --> 00:23:16,480
Couldn't let myself to go

339
00:23:16,480 --> 00:23:21,250
Even though I feel

340
00:23:21,250 --> 00:23:27,150
The end

341
00:23:46,110 --> 00:23:51,640
Full moon sways

342
00:23:52,950 --> 00:23:59,980
Smiling in my arms for all those years

343
00:24:13,730 --> 00:24:15,570
We're finally headed North.

344
00:24:15,570 --> 00:24:16,270
Destination: Grateful Sound!

345
00:24:16,270 --> 00:24:17,400
"Live 22 'Performance Eve Festival"'

346
00:24:16,270 --> 00:24:17,400
Destination: Grateful Sound!

347
00:24:17,400 --> 00:24:20,170
"Live 22 'Performance Eve Festival"'

348
00:24:17,400 --> 00:24:20,170
Next episode, Performance Eve Festival!
Watch it, okay?
